,"tiePercentage":0}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"3965","guid":"d3d4014b-0c69-3e7a-a5e4-d84b92d3de15","fullName":"Broadview Stadium","address":{"city":"Buffalo","state":"NY","zipCode":"14228","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/college-football/day/interior/3965.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day","interior"]}]},"attendance":5452},"article":{"headline":"Burch hits 200 yards again and Buffalo wins 6th straight, 40-21 over Central Michigan","description":"— Messiah Burch ran for 200 yards and scored twice for the second consecutive game and Buffalo won its sixth-straight game 40-21 over Central Michigan on Wednesday night.","story":"BUFFALO, N.Y. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5151369/messiah-burch\" target=\"_new\">Messiah Burch</a> ran for 200 yards and scored twice for the second consecutive game and Buffalo won its sixth-straight game 40-21 over Central Michigan on Wednesday night.\n\n\r\n              Burch had exactly 200 yards, giving him 1,310 for the season. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://x.com/UBuffaloFB/status/2123246487089938631\">Burch's 75-yard burst up the middle</a> was the backbreaker, coming one play after the Chippewas pulled within 26-21 with 3:55 to play in the third quarter. He also scored on a 10-yard run.\n\n\r\n              Buffalo (8-3, 6-1 Mid-American Conference), which has its longest winning streak since winning seven-straight in 2013, piled up 283 yards on the ground. Terrance Shelton had 81 yards and a touchdown and quarterback <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4077876/jason-wright\" target=\"_new\">Jason Wright</a> also scored on the ground.\n\n\r\n              Wright had a 17-yard toss to <a href=\"https://x.com/UBuffaloFB/status/2123234157765533866\"><a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4869601/chance-morrow\" target=\"_new\">Chance Morrow</a>, who had a spectacular catch</a> for his 10th receiving touchdown this season. That came with 10 seconds in the first half and allowed Buffalo to take a 20-14 lead just 33 seconds after Central Michigan took a 14-13 lead.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5149056/jadyn-glasser\" target=\"_new\">Jadyn Glasser</a> threw three touchdown passes for the Chippewas (5-6, 3-4) but was intercepted twice.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Central Michigan: at Ball State on Nov. 28.\n\n\r\n              Buffalo: at Akron on No. 27.\n\n\r\n              ——-\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>. Visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here.</a>","published":"2026-11-19T03:58:33Z"}}